From 538552322e6e1a590b0e4270ec56c7daf05265e9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: exeroom536 <352890649+exeroom536@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 06:57:11 +0500
Subject: [PATCH 30/32] super-amd: grow a RAIDABLE volume into a RAID1

RAIDABLE is a volume of one disk kept for a future mirror; the AMD
driver makes it a RAID1 by a migration.  With subarray_raid_disks:

- mdadm --grow <RAIDABLE> --raid-devices=2 gives the md raid1 a second
  slot, mdmon takes a spare for it (a dedicated, then a global one) and
  records the migration as the AMD driver does: the transform log first,
  then the configuration with both LDs; when md has copied the mirror,
  the RAID1 alone;
- a migration the AMD driver started is assembled and finished by mdmon
  from its log; --examine shows its progress;
- --raid-devices=1 takes the second slot back after a migration that
  failed.

container_content() now gives the spares a volume may take, which Grow
checks --raid-devices against.  The other AMD migrations (level, stripe
and size changes) are not supported; a volume in one is not started.

Written by Claude Opus 5.5, an AI model by Anthropic.
